# Rule Engine — Test Data & Calculation Guide

## 1. Rule Engine Overview

The Rule Engine calculates pay and bill amounts for timesheets. It evaluates up to 6 rule types in strict priority order, allocating worked hours to the highest-priority applicable rule first.

### Core Principles

- **Unallocated hours paid (when enabled)**: Hours not covered by any rule are unallocated. When `isUnplannedHoursPayEnabled: 1`, these are paid at 1x rate.
- **No overlap**: Range-based rules cannot overlap on the same day.
- **Priority-based allocation**: Higher-priority rules claim hours first.
- **Threshold-based OT**: Daily/Weekly OT use total-hours thresholds, not time ranges.
- **Break applies everywhere**: Break logic applies across all range-based rules.

### Rule Priority Order

| Priority | Rule | Type | Claims |
|----------|------|------|--------|
| 1 (highest) | Regular Hours | Range-based | Scheduled time range (effective hours) |
| 2 | Before Shift (BS) | Range-based | 12 AM → entered time |
| 3 | After Shift (AS) | Range-based | Entered time → 12 AM |
| 4 | Specific Hours Range (SR) | Range-based | User-defined start–end |
| 5 | Daily Overtime (DOT) | Threshold-based | Unallocated hours (daily threshold) |
| 6 (lowest) | Weekly Overtime (WOT) | Threshold-based | Remaining unallocated (weekly threshold) |

### Rule Multiplicity Constraints

| Rule | Instances Allowed | Notes |
|------|-------------------|-------|
| Regular Hours | Always 1 (system rule) | Cannot be removed |
| Before Shift | **1 per day** | Cannot apply twice on same day |
| After Shift | **1 per day** | Cannot apply twice on same day |
| Specific Hours Range | **Multiple allowed** | Non-overlapping ranges, each with own multiplier |
| Daily Overtime | **Multiple tiers allowed** | Each threshold must be unique per day |
| Weekly Overtime | **Only 1 instance** | Single tier, applies to all 7 days |

