## 7. Rule 6 — Weekly Overtime (Priority 6)

### How WOT Works
WOT is the **lowest priority** threshold-based rule. It claims remaining unallocated hours after ALL other rules (including DOT) have claimed.

### Key Constraints
- **Only 1 instance** allowed (no tiered WOT).
- Applies to **all 7 days** (auto-selected, cannot be changed).
- Only for weekly and biweekly timesheets.
- Threshold minimum = sum of all scheduled daily hours.

### WOT Threshold Check
```
weekly_toward = sum of daily toward values across entire week
WOT_hours = min(weekly_toward − WOT_threshold, total_weekly_unallocated)
```

### Day Off / Weekend Work
On non-working days:
- No regular hours → all work is unallocated.
- DOT applies per-day (if configured for that day and threshold met).
- WOT accumulates weekly — weekend unallocated hours flow to WOT if weekly threshold met.

### Weekend-Specific Pattern
```
DOT can apply any day but checks per-day threshold.
WOT must apply all 7 days and checks weekly total.

Scenario: Mon-Fri 9-17(8h), DOT>10, WOT>40
Weekend Sat 9-15(6h): DOT: 6 NOT>10 → CLOSED. All 6h → WOT pool.
Weekend Sun 9-13(4h): DOT: 4 NOT>10 → CLOSED. All 4h → WOT pool.
Weekly toward=50>40 → WOT claims min(10, 10) = 10h from weekend.
```

### rulesApplied Format
```
WeeklyOT:[multiplier: 2, threshold:>40, appliedDay:[mon,tue,wed,thu,fri,sat,sun]]
```

### weeklyOT Field Format (separate from acceptedPayBillRate)
```
"weeklyOT": "Week1:[pay, bill]"
```

