## 8. Unallocated Hours (New Enhancement)

### Definition
**Unallocated hours** are worked hours that are NOT claimed by any configured rule:
- NOT within Regular Hours (or effective regular for BPN)
- NOT within Before Shift range
- NOT within After Shift range
- NOT within Specific Hours Range
- NOT claimed by Daily Overtime
- NOT claimed by Weekly Overtime

### When Unallocated Hours Occur

| Scenario | Example | Unallocated |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| Gap between BS and Regular | BS ends 7:00, Reg starts 9:00, work 6:00-10:00 | 7:00-9:00 = 2h |
| Gap between Regular and AS | Reg ends 17:00, AS starts 19:00, work 16:00-20:00 | 17:00-19:00 = 2h |
| Work outside all ranges | Reg 9-17, no other rules, work 17:00-19:00 | 17:00-19:00 = 2h |
| BPN freed hours (ant > actual break) | ant=2h, no break taken | 2h freed → unallocated |
| Hours helping meet OT threshold | Work 10h, DOT>8, effective_reg=6 | 2h toward threshold = unallocated |
| DOT gate closed | Work 8h, DOT>8 | 8 NOT > 8, all excess = unallocated |
| Weekend/day-off (no reg hours) | dayPattern excludes Sat, work Sat 9-15, no DOT/WOT met | 6h unallocated |

### isUnplannedHoursPayEnabled Flag

| Value | Behavior |
|-------|----------|
| `0` (default) | Unallocated hours are **unpaid** (original behavior) |
| `1` | Unallocated hours are **paid at 1x rate** (same as regular hours) |

This flag is set in:
- `/v1/rule-engine/rule-template` endpoint
- `/v1/timesheet-settings` endpoint

### Unallocated Hours Calculation

```
unallocated = total_worked − actual_break − regular_paid − BS_hours − AS_hours − SR_hours − DOT_hours − WOT_hours
```

Or equivalently:
```
unallocated = gap_hours + freed_hours − (hours claimed by DOT/WOT from pool)
```

### Pay Calculation (when enabled)
```
Unallocated Pay = unallocated_hours × payRate × 1
Unallocated Bill = unallocated_hours × billRate × 1
```

### acceptedPayBillRate Format (with unallocatedHours)
```
"Mon:[regularHours:[8,16], unallocatedHours:[2,4]]"
"Mon:[beforeShift:[3,6], regularHours:[6,12], unallocatedHours:[4,8]]"
```

**IMPORTANT**: Always include `unallocatedHours:[0,0]` even when zero for consistency in test data when `isUnplannedHoursPayEnabled: 1`.

### Examples

**Example 1: Gap between BS and Regular**
```
Regular: 9:00-17:00, BS: 7:00 (range 00:00-7:00)
Work: 6:00-10:00 (4h)
BS: 6:00-7:00 = 1h
Gap (unallocated): 7:00-9:00 = 2h
Regular: 9:00-10:00 = 1h
Total: 1h BS + 2h unalloc + 1h reg = 4h
```

**Example 2: BPN freed hours become unallocated**
```
Regular: 9:00-17:00, anticipated=2h, no break taken
Work: 9:00-19:00 (10h)
effective_reg = 8-2 = 6h
reg_paid = 6h
freed = anticipated - actual_break = 2 - 0 = 2h
Outside regular (17-19) = 2h
unallocated = freed(2) + outside(2) = 4h
```

**Example 3: Hours helping meet DOT threshold**
```
Regular: 9:00-17:00, DOT>8, anticipated=2h
Work: 9:00-19:00 (10h), no break
effective_reg = 8-2 = 6h
toward = 10 > 8 → DOT excess = 2h
But DOT can only claim from outside-regular pool = 2h (17-19)
DOT claims 2h
freed = 2h (ant=2, no break)
unallocated = freed = 2h (helps meet threshold but not paid as DOT)
```

