## 15. Edge Case Checklist

When generating test data, always consider:

### Threshold Boundaries
- [ ] Exactly AT threshold (gate closed: `N NOT > N`)
- [ ] Just above threshold (gate opens: `N+0.01 > N`)
- [ ] Well below threshold
- [ ] Well above threshold

### Work Patterns
- [ ] Single entry covering all zones
- [ ] Multiple entries no gap (back-to-back)
- [ ] Multiple entries with gap (unworked time between entries)
- [ ] Entries spanning (gap in regular zone)
- [ ] 3+ entries (before + during + after regular)
- [ ] Work only in gap zone (no regular covered)
- [ ] Work only before regular hours
- [ ] Work only after regular hours

### Multi-Day / Weekly
- [ ] Mon-Fri uniform (same hours each day)
- [ ] Mon-Fri mixed (different hours per day)
- [ ] Weekend only (day off, no regular hours)
- [ ] Weekday + weekend (WOT accumulation)
- [ ] Full 7-day work week
- [ ] DOT met on some days but not others
- [ ] DOT never met but WOT met (weekend contributes)

### Break Scenarios (BPN)
- [ ] break = anticipated (freed=0)
- [ ] No break, anticipated > 0 (freed=ant)
- [ ] break < anticipated (partial freed)
- [ ] break > anticipated (no freed, reg reduced)
- [ ] Break in gap zone (outside regular)
- [ ] Break drops below all thresholds
- [ ] Anticipated excess helps DOT/WOT
- [ ] Multi-day with varying break patterns

### DOT + WOT Specific
- [ ] Both triggered
- [ ] DOT only (WOT threshold too high)
- [ ] WOT only (DOT threshold too high / gate closed)
- [ ] Neither triggered (both thresholds too high)
- [ ] DOT eats all unallocated (WOT starved)
- [ ] DOT barely opens (WOT gets majority)
- [ ] Weekend hours all→WOT (DOT not met per-day)
- [ ] Short regular hours (e.g., 9-12 = 3h) creating large gaps

### Unallocated Hours Scenarios (isUnplannedHoursPayEnabled: 1)
- [ ] Gap between BS and Regular (BS ends before regular starts)
- [ ] Gap between Regular and AS (AS starts after regular ends)
- [ ] Work outside all configured ranges (no rule covers time)
- [ ] BPN freed hours become unallocated (anticipated > actual break)
- [ ] DOT gate closed (toward ≤ threshold) — excess becomes unallocated
- [ ] Hours helping meet DOT/WOT threshold (counted but not OT-paid)
- [ ] Weekend work with no DOT/WOT rules (all hours unallocated)
- [ ] Full day unallocated (no regular hours, no rules match)
- [ ] Partial unallocated (some hours claimed by rules, some not)
- [ ] Zero unallocated (all worked hours claimed by rules)
- [ ] Multiple days with varying unallocated amounts
- [ ] Unallocated + DOT combination
- [ ] Unallocated + WOT combination
- [ ] Unallocated with complex rule combinations (BS+AS+SR+DOT+WOT)

